  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compute differences between outcomes and a reference value (zero in this case), then evaluate the mean difference weighted by probability. Both lotteries have the same mean difference (6 Euros), so the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not mention any such calculation or reference value. Instead, the justification is based on the prize amount and a subjective assessment that the 0.1% difference in probability is negligible. There is no evidence of considering differences from a reference value or applying the rule of comparing weighted mean differences. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reasoning is entirely different — it is based on prize size and risk tolerance, not on the formal rule of mean differences from a reference value. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
